>>
Rule 1 (input must be a tensor-like object to support abs; prevents numpy scalar usage)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (boolean tensors are not supported by abs)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 3 (Softsign expects a numeric tensor dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 4 (each dimension size of the input tensor is non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
